We start with coffee as twelve: coffee = 12
and a mug as five: mug = 5
and beans as eight: beans = 8
then we pack them into an inventory: inventory = { "coffee" => !-3, "mug" => !-2, "beans" => !-1 }

We print the items in order.

inventory.sort.each do |name, count|
  puts "#{name}: #{count}"
end

and we total the counts: total = inventory.values.reduce(0) { |sum, count| sum + count }
then we show the total: puts !-1
